# `fj` CLI — Forgejo

Forgejo's CLI (`fj`) is installed via Homebrew as a standalone binary. It auto-detects the remote host from the git remote in the current directory.

See **[docs/fj-guide.md](../../docs/fj-guide.md)** for the full command reference (issues, PRs, conventions).

## Remote detection

`fj` reads the git remote URL from the current repo. Local Cove remotes use `https://git.cove/<owner>/<repo>.git`. The `cove-push` token in git's credential helper handles auth (set up by `cove up`).

SSH (`git@forgejo-localhost:...`) is also available as an optional transport — see `~/.agents/agents-md-detail/cove.md` for SSH config details.

## HTTPS auth

`cove up` caches a persistent API token (`cove-push`) in git's credential helper so `fj` can push over HTTPS without prompting.

## Draft / Ready status

Forgejo uses the PR title to determine draft status:

- **Draft:** title starts with `WIP:` (case-insensitive) — PR **cannot** be merged
- **Ready:** title does **not** start with `WIP:`

```bash
# Create a draft PR
fj pr create "WIP: my change"

# Mark ready (remove WIP: prefix)
fj pr edit <PR> title "my change"

# Mark draft (add WIP: prefix)
fj pr edit <PR> title "WIP: my change"
```

## Checking CI status

```bash
fj actions tasks
```

## PR comments

```bash
# View all comments on a PR
fj pr view <PR#> comments

# View a specific comment by index (0-indexed)
fj pr view <PR#> comment <IDX>
```

